1. OWNERSHIP. The copyright holder of this software, including its source code,
   documentation and accompanying materials (the "Software"), is the person
   named above (the "Owner"). This document transfers no ownership and grants no
   rights beyond those expressly stated in sections 2 and 5. All rights not
   expressly granted are reserved.

2. WHAT IS ALLOWED. The Owner grants any person who lawfully receives a copy of
   the Software (the "User") a personal, revocable, non-exclusive and
   non-transferable permission to (a) install and run the Software for their own
   non-commercial purposes, (b) read and study its source code, and (c) make
   backup copies of their own installation. Reproduction is limited to what is
   strictly necessary for those three uses. Non-commercial means use from which
   no income, consideration or economic benefit is obtained, directly or
   indirectly, and which is not part of the activity of a business or
   professional. The legal form of the entity is not decisive: what matters is
   the actual use made of the Software.

3. WHAT IS NOT ALLOWED without the Owner's prior written permission: (a)
   commercial use; (b) modifying, adapting, translating or transforming the
   Software, or creating derivative works from it; (c) reproducing or copying
   the Software beyond what is indispensable to install, run and back it up
   under section 2; (d) distributing, publishing, assigning, selling, renting,
   lending, uploading to repositories or services accessible by third parties,
   or otherwise making the Software or any part of it, including its source
   code, available; (e) sublicensing or transferring the permissions granted
   here; (f) decompiling, disassembling or reverse engineering the Software, or
   attempting to obtain its source code from a compiled version, except where
   mandatory law allows it and only for the purposes that law contemplates; (g)
   removing, hiding or altering authorship, copyright or licence notices in the
   Software, its source code, its interface or its documentation.

4. REQUESTING PERMISSION. Any of the above, including commercial use, may be
   authorised. Write to mateof@gmail.com describing the intended use. Permission,
   if granted, will be in writing and may carry conditions.

5. PATENTS. For the uses permitted in section 2, and only for those, the Owner
   also grants a licence to the patents it can license and that would be
   infringed by using the Software. This patent licence ends immediately if the
   User, or the company they work for, claims in writing that the Software
   infringes or contributes to infringing a patent.

6. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS. The Software uses third-party libraries distributed
   under their own licences, which are unaffected by this document.

7. TERM, CURE AND TERMINATION. This licence remains in force while its
   conditions are met. The first time the Owner gives written notice of a
   breach, the licence continues if the User fully corrects it and takes
   reasonable steps to remedy what has been done within 32 days of the notice.
   Otherwise, and for any later breach, the licence terminates automatically
   without notice, and the User must stop using the Software and destroy any
   copies held.

8. NO WARRANTY. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
   EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

9. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW,
   THE OWNER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY
   ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE.

10. GOVERNING LAW. Spanish law governs this licence.
